        "score": 0.03278689,
        "excerpt": "to control a well on cyclical production, or where frequent changes in production\nrate are necessary.\n(3)\non wells which are frequently subject to shutdown.\n3.2.1  Positive or Fixed Choke\nThis normally consists of two parts:\n(1)\nA choke which consists of a machined housing into which the orifice capability\nor \"bean\" is installed.\n(2)\nA \"bean\" which consists of a short length 1-6\", of thick walled tube with a\nsmooth, machined bore of specified size.\nThe assembly is shown in Figure 32.\n                                      \nFixed \nOrifice\nDirection of Flow\nFigure 32\nFixed choke"
      },
